  "lore": {
    "relay": {
      "note": "A1 §5.2: ~190 km of ridge-line and road, towers sited for line of sight at 8–10 km spacing → 21–24 relay towers, plus one tower in each of the six towns. A1 §7.1 calls the tower chain the map's actual subject, so it carries the sheet's single accent colour (bell-bronze).",
      "spacingKm": 8,
      "owner": "the Bellfaith",
      "derivation": "Towers were sampled at even intervals along the spine (Gildmark → Embervale → Millcross → Rooktide, 182 km — A1's '~190 km of ridge-line and road') and along the flat crossing, then frozen here as explicit coordinates. Sight-line spans are 7.8–8.4 km, inside A1 §5.2's 8–10 km line-of-sight budget. 27 towers are drawn: 22 on the ridgelines and roads (A1 says 21–24) plus 5 town towers. Cindervast has none — A1 §7.2: the Bellfaith will not draw a city it does not ring.",
      "withheld": "A1 §7.2: the far-mirror stations sit on these same ridgelines and are deliberately NOT drawn — a Bellfaith map will not publish a Gildmark monopoly it cannot regulate.",
      "amendedPending": "AMENDED-PENDING (I-095): note/derivation above cite pre-F-045 absolute km (190 km ridge-line, 8–10 km tower spacing, 182 km spine, 7.8–8.4 km sight-line spans) — the actual tower coordinates already sit on the rescaled 400 km world; this prose re-voice is deferred."
    },
    "distances": {
      "paceKmPerDay": 30,
      "paceKmPerHour": 11,
      "drawnRoadsAreCentrelines": "roads[].points is a simplified centre-line, so its measured length runs 0–15% short of roads[].roadKm (A1 §5.1's surveyed figure). The day-counts lettered on the sheet come from roadKm/days, never from the drawn length.",
      "note": "A1 §5.1. `straightKm` is the Cartographer's figure; `computedKm` is what this file's own coordinates give, and `deltaPct` is the residual. A1 §5.3: the world preserves topology, not metric distance.",
      "amendedPending": "AMENDED-PENDING (I-095): paceKmPerDay, drawnRoadsAreCentrelines and note above describe the pre-F-045 day-count travel model — distances are now hour-scale on the 400 km world (paceKmPerHour: 11). Prose re-voice deferred."
    }
  },
